abstract: >-
  An interactive bilingual (Turkish/English) study of how knowledge is transmitted
  between generations, built on a six-link transmission chain — packet, decoder,
  context, tacit knowledge, apparatus, maintenance — and tested against 32 real
  objects drawn from the modern-industrial, Ottoman and Roman worlds, with 255 dated
  and individually sourced events. The repository also contains the link-coded corpus
  as CSV and JSON with a codebook. The study is a synthesis and a teaching instrument,
  not a research contribution: it has not been through human peer review and was
  produced with AI assistance, and both facts are stated in the work itself.
keywords:
  - knowledge transmission
  - cultural evolution
  - digital preservation
  - tacit knowledge
  - OAIS
  - maintenance studies
  - language endangerment
  - interactive explanation
